# public/_redirects: the one-hop 301/410 map for nocoturf.com. The table with the reason for every
# line, the holds and the off-domain work is docs/REDIRECTS.md. tests/redirects.test.mjs checks this file
# (run it with LAUNCH_CHECK=1 after `npm run build` to also check that every target exists in dist/).
#
# How Netlify reads this file (docs.netlify.com/manage/routing/redirects/, checked 2026-09-24):
# - It reads this file before the netlify.toml rules, top to bottom, and the first match wins.
# - It matches a path with or without its trailing slash, so ONE line covers /x and /x/. Never write a
#   rule that only adds or removes a slash: it loops. Pretty URLs (on by default) sends /about to /about/.
# - A built file at a source path beats a rule without "!", so a real page always wins over its old rule.
#   The only forced rule is /index.html, which exists as a file.
# - Paths are case-sensitive. A query string passes through to a 301 target.
# - A 410 line serves the body of /404.html with status 410, and the URL stays the same.
#
# Every 301 goes to an absolute https://www.nocoturf.com/ URL so an old apex (nocoturf.com) URL lands on its
# new page in ONE hop, without first bouncing to www. Never send an old URL to the homepage in bulk.
# Service URLs here must match the `legacy` arrays in src/data/services.ts: change that file first.

